# "When this creature enters, you may sacrifice an artifact. When you do, this creature deals 3 damage to any target" (CR 701.21a,
# 603.12, 120.2b). Bot1 sacrifices Mox Jet (a noncreature artifact) as the enter trigger resolves, and the reflexive trigger that
# follows deals exactly 3 to Bot2. The Crook itself is not an artifact and may not be chosen, and only one artifact may be
# sacrificed ("an artifact"): the two Ornithopters together are refused.

[Bot1 Deck]
Cornered Crook
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Mountain x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Cornered Crook.Cast
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Choose(Cornered Crook)
! Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter; Ornithopter)
Bot1.Choose(Mox Jet)
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Graveyard = Mox Jet
Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Cornered Crook.Power = 5
Bot1.Battlefield.Cornered Crook.Toughness = 4
